!theme plain
title FP Error Handling and Recovery Scenarios

participant "Client App" as Client
participant "FP Dispatcher" as Dispatcher
participant "Session Manager" as SessionMgr
participant "Transport" as Transport
participant "Server App" as Server

== Scenario 1: Invalid Arguments ==
Client -> Dispatcher: fp_disp_client_send_req(NULL, ...)
activate Dispatcher
note over Dispatcher: Validate parameters
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_INVARGS
deactivate Dispatcher

== Scenario 2: Session Pool Exhausted ==
Client -> Dispatcher: fp_disp_client_send_req(...)
activate Dispatcher
Dispatcher -> SessionMgr: fp_disp_session_mgr_open_session()
activate SessionMgr
note over SessionMgr: All sessions in use
SessionMgr -> Dispatcher: NULL (no available session)
deactivate SessionMgr
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_NO_MEM
deactivate Dispatcher

== Scenario 3: Transport Send Failure ==
Client -> Dispatcher: fp_disp_client_send_req(...)
activate Dispatcher
Dispatcher -> SessionMgr: [Session allocated successfully]
Dispatcher -> Transport: (*p_fp_send)(&ctx)
activate Transport
note over Transport: Network/hardware failure
Transport -> Dispatcher: false (send failed)
deactivate Transport
Dispatcher -> SessionMgr: [Close session]
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_SENDERR
deactivate Dispatcher

== Scenario 4: Response Timeout ==
Client -> Dispatcher: fp_disp_client_send_req(..., timeout=5000)
activate Dispatcher
Dispatcher -> Transport: [Send successful]
note over Dispatcher: Start timeout tracking
... 5000ms elapsed ...
note over SessionMgr: Timer expires
SessionMgr -> SessionMgr: [Auto-close session]
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_TIMEOUT
deactivate Dispatcher

== Scenario 5: Unsupported Function ==
Client -> Dispatcher: [Request sent successfully]
Dispatcher -> Transport: [Forward to server]
Transport -> Server: [Request received]
activate Server
note over Server: Function not implemented
Server -> Transport: FP_CMD_STATUS_FUNC_NOT_SUPPORTED
deactivate Server
Transport -> Dispatcher: [Response received]
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_FUNC_NOT_SUPPORTED

== Scenario 6: ARM-and-FIRE Data Integrity Error ==
Client -> Dispatcher: [ARM request sent]
Dispatcher -> Server: [ARM processed, session created]
Server -> Dispatcher: FP_CMD_STATUS_ARMED
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_ARMED

note over Client: User modifies request data
Client -> Dispatcher: [FIRE request with modified data]
Dispatcher -> Server: [FIRE request]
activate Server
note over Server: Hash mismatch detected\nnew_hash != stored_hash
Server -> Dispatcher: FP_CMD_STATUS_DATA_INTEGRITY_ERR
deactivate Server
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_DATA_INTEGRITY_ERR
note over Server: Session remains active\nfor potential retry

== Scenario 7: ARM-and-FIRE Timeout ==
Client -> Dispatcher: [ARM request sent]
Dispatcher -> Server: [ARM processed]
Server -> Dispatcher: FP_CMD_STATUS_ARMED
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_ARMED

note over Server: 15 minutes elapse
note over SessionMgr: Automatic session cleanup
SessionMgr -> SessionMgr: [Close server session]

Client -> Dispatcher: [FIRE request sent after timeout]
Dispatcher -> Server: [FIRE request]
activate Server
note over Server: No active session found
Server -> Dispatcher: FP_CMD_STATUS_FUNC_NOT_SUPPORTED
deactivate Server
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_FUNC_NOT_SUPPORTED

== Scenario 8: Lock Timeout ==
Client -> Dispatcher: fp_disp_client_send_req(...)
activate Dispatcher
Dispatcher -> SessionMgr: fp_disp_session_mgr_open_session()
activate SessionMgr
note over SessionMgr: fp_arch_lock_section() timeout
SessionMgr -> Dispatcher: NULL (lock failed)
deactivate SessionMgr
Dispatcher -> Client: FP_CMD_STATUS_NO_MEM
deactivate Dispatcher

note right of Dispatcher
  Error Recovery Strategies:
  - Graceful degradation
  - Resource cleanup
  - Session auto-recovery
  - Timeout protection
  - Status code propagation
end note

note right of SessionMgr
  Session Protection:
  - Automatic timeout cleanup
  - Resource leak prevention
  - Thread-safe operations
  - Metrics tracking
  - Error state handling
end note

@enduml
